VABAR runs on RoboSimStudio (https://github.com/robosimstudio/robosimstudio),
Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 Kaiyuan Chen, installed as a dependency.
vabar/_upstream/bench_run.py is RoboSimStudio's scripts/bench_run.py, copied
unmodified because the RoboSimStudio wheel does not ship its scripts/.

This distribution includes third-party robot models. Each keeps its own
licence, in a LICENSE file beside the files it covers:

assets/embodiments/robotiq_2f85/
    Robotiq 2F-85 gripper, from MuJoCo Menagerie
    (https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie). BSD 2-Clause
    License. Copyright (c) 2013, ROS-Industrial.

assets/embodiments/ur5/
    Universal Robots UR5, from ROS-Industrial universal_robot. BSD 3-Clause
    License. Copyright 2018 ROS Industrial Consortium.

assets/embodiments/yam/i2rt_yam/
assets/embodiments/yam_i2rt/
assets/embodiments/linear_4310/
    i2rt YAM arm and linear_4310 gripper (https://github.com/i2rt-robotics/i2rt).
    MIT License. Copyright (c) I2RT Robotics.

assets/embodiments/panda/
    Franka Emika Panda kinematics, identical to the file RoboSimStudio ships;
    see RoboSimStudio's NOTICE for its provenance (robosuite, MIT;
    example-robot-data, BSD 3-Clause; franka_description, Apache 2.0).

Object meshes, fixtures and scans are listed with their sources, and with the
licences still to be confirmed, in ASSET_PROVENANCE.md.
